The files dinara_align/alignment.mojo, dinara_align/common.mojo and
dinara_align/errors.mojo derive from AffineGaps' alignment.mojo, common.mojo and
errors.mojo, and have been changed since: the folding, cofolding, protein-scoring,
Python-binding and command-line code was removed, the sources were migrated to
Mojo 1.1, the device specs query gained a branch for Apple GPUs, which Metal
answers only in part, and the host sweeps, traceback and linear-space recursion
were extended and vectorized. dinara_align/scoring.mojo keeps parts of the
dispatch and batch packing of AffineGaps' affinegaps.mojo, rewritten from Python
objects to native Mojo types. Each of these files says so in its header.

The unit-cost edit distance, dinara_align/bit_parallel.mojo, diagonal.mojo,
seeds.mojo, band.mojo, traceback.mojo, edit_distance.mojo, edit_search.mojo and
slides.mojo, is ported from pa-bitpacking in A*PA
(https://github.com/RagnarGrootKoerkamp/astar-pairwise-aligner, commit
bf2e14e0cbc3a9a03600dcda0641d7f89e401e63), by Ragnar Groot Koerkamp and Pesho
Ivanov, licensed under the Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0.

